1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,705
The numbers hid the water itself.

2
00:00:01,705 --> 00:00:18,041
Into the file went a well of readings, a bed of sediment, and an element of weather that no instrument had recorded; the atmosphere of the field station was almost cheerful, and the condition of the river was not.

3
00:00:18,041 --> 00:00:23,320
The main product of the process was a clean record of the wrong question.

4
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:28,609
“We give the river a channel and call it data,” the boatman said.

5
00:00:28,609 --> 00:00:41,456
“The land, the forest, and the native trees are not in your table.” The male and female volunteers agreed on that, and the food for the meeting was an eggplant stew.

6
00:00:41,456 --> 00:00:48,084
The root of the problem was a lock on the model: only one kind of evidence could get in.

7
00:00:48,084 --> 00:01:01,271
A stream of dust from the dock, a pot of cotton, and a mineral sample in a pad of wax: the craft of the old survey was precise and blind to the river bed.

8
00:01:01,271 --> 00:01:13,713
The spray from the washing of the trap, the rip in the organ pipe, and the screw that nobody could find: the establishment had replaced a measurement with a maintenance schedule.

9
00:01:13,713 --> 00:01:19,452
“We are against the light of a single number,” Maya said.

10
00:01:19,452 --> 00:01:29,039
The calling of the volunteers was to look at the earth and the ocean in the same hour, with the same need to know and the same willingness to be wrong.

11
00:01:29,039 --> 00:01:37,723
A rib of the old dam, a gum tree, and a calorie table were not enough to explain a flood.

12
00:01:37,723 --> 00:01:43,561
While the report was being written, the river went down and came back up.

13
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:53,789
The numbers hid that too, and the group agreed to publish the whole page, similar in shape to the first one but with a ground line at the bottom.

14
00:01:53,789 --> 00:02:00,467
The dust, the pot, the pad, and the spray: all of it was ours.

15
00:02:00,467 --> 00:02:17,178
“The river gives us the question,” the boatman said, “and the establishment gives us the form.” The stream, the lock, the dock, and the trap were all in the same chapter, and the craft of the survey was to see them together.

16
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:28,229
The air, the star, and the nature of the river were not in the drug of a single number; either we play fairly or we do not play at all.
